# Setting up the backend

## 1: Create and Navigate to the Project Directory

```bash
mkdir med-vision-inspector
cd med-vision-inspector
```

## 2: Create Folder Structure

Set up the internal folder hierarchy for the FastAPI backend:

```bash
mkdir -p backend/app/api backend/app/core backend/app/models
```

## 3: Create a .gitignore File

Create a .gitignore file in the root directory to keep unnecessary files (like virtual environments and caches) out of Git:

```bash
touch .gitignore
```

(Paste the standard Python/Angular ignore rules into this file).

## 4: Create and Activate a Python Virtual Environment

Create an isolated virtual environment inside the project and activate it:

On Windows (PowerShell):

```bash
python -m venv backend/venv
.\backend\venv\Scripts\Activate
```

On macOS / Linux:

```bash
python3 -m venv backend/venv
source backend/venv/bin/activate
```

## 5: Create Dependencies File (requirements.txt)

Create the requirements file inside the backend folder:

```bash
touch backend/requirements.txt
```

Add the required packages into backend/requirements.txt:

```text
fastapi==0.110.0
uvicorn==0.28.0
torch==2.2.0
torchvision==0.17.0
numpy==1.26.4
opencv-python==4.9.0.80
pillow==10.2.0
python-multipart==0.0.9
```

## 6: Install Dependencies

Run pip to install all necessary libraries inside a virtual environment:

```bash
pip install -r backend/requirements.txt
```

## 7: Create the Main Application File main.py inside backend/app/:

```bash
touch backend/app/main.py
```

(Populate main.py with the FastAPI application code we prepared earlier for image processing and heatmap generation).

## 8: Run the Backend Server

Start FastAPI development server with hot-reload enabled:

```bash
uvicorn backend.app.main:app --reload
```

or

```bash
docker-compose up --build
```

Once running, open the browser and navigate to [http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs) to see the interactive Swagger UI and test image inspection endpoint!
